steps.body:
A **deque**, a double-ended queue, adds and removes at both ends. JavaScript has none, but an array covers what a window needs: `push` and `pop` work the back, and a `head` index is the front, as in a queue.

To find the **maximum of every window** of `k` items, keep the indexes of the current window in the deque, their values going down from front to back. Then the front is the window's maximum:

1. Before adding index `i`, pop from the back every index whose value is not bigger than `nums[i]`. It can never be a maximum again, since `nums[i]` is at least as big and stays in the window longer.
2. Push `i`.
3. If the front index has slid out of the window, `dq[head] <= i - k`, move `head` on.
4. Once the first window is full, `i >= k - 1`, `nums[dq[head]]` is its maximum.

```javascript
const nums = [4, 2, 12, 3, 8, 1, 9];
const k = 3;
const dq = []; // indexes, values falling from front to back
let head = 0; // the front of dq
const maxes = [];
for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
  while (dq.length > head && nums[dq.at(-1)] <= nums[i]) {
    dq.pop();
  }
  dq.push(i);
  if (dq[head] <= i - k) {
    head++;
  }
  if (i >= k - 1) {
    maxes.push(nums[dq[head]]);
  }
}
console.log(maxes.join(" ")); // 12 12 12 8 9
```

The deque is the part of `dq` from `head` on, so it is empty when `dq.length === head`. Each index is pushed once and leaves at most once, from the back or the front, so the scan is O(n). Calling `Math.max` on every window would be O(n * k).

example.code:
const input = require("fs").readFileSync(0, "utf8");
const [kLine, loadLine] = input.trim().split("\n");
const k = Number(kLine);
const load = loadLine.trim().split(/\s+/).map(Number);

const dq = []; // indexes, loads falling from front to back
let head = 0; // the front of dq
for (let i = 0; i < load.length; i++) {
  while (dq.length > head && load[dq.at(-1)] <= load[i]) {
    dq.pop(); // can never be a peak again
  }
  dq.push(i);
  if (dq[head] <= i - k) {
    head++; // the front slid out of the window
  }
  if (i >= k - 1) {
    console.log(`Minutes ${i - k + 2}-${i + 1}: peak ${load[dq[head]]}`);
  }
}

